# cron.example — Schwab MCP health probe scheduling

Pick the snippet matching your operating system and customize the path
substitutions (`UV_BIN`, `REPO`).

The probe schedule is biased toward the user's typical "active windows"
(STRATEGY.md §2 — weekend evening + mid-week evening) so a near-expiry
warning lands when there is a realistic chance the user is at the keyboard.
A 4-hour fallback handles laptops that were closed during a scheduled run.

---

## macOS (launchd)

Save as `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.kevinkda.schwab-marketdata-mcp.health.plist`,
then load with:

```bash
launchctl load -w ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.kevinkda.schwab-marketdata-mcp.health.plist
```

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.kevinkda.schwab-marketdata-mcp.health</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/YOURUSER/.local/bin/uv</string>
        <string>--directory</string>
        <string>/Users/YOURUSER/code/kevinkda/schwab-marketdata-mcp</string>
        <string>run</string>
        <string>python</string>
        <string>-m</string>
        <string>schwab_marketdata_mcp.health</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Primary cadence: Sunday 20:00 + Wednesday 21:00 (24h clock). -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>Weekday</key><integer>0</integer>  <!-- Sunday -->
            <key>Hour</key><integer>20</integer>
            <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>Weekday</key><integer>3</integer>  <!-- Wednesday -->
            <key>Hour</key><integer>21</integer>
            <key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer>
        </dict>
    </array>

    <!-- Lid-close fallback: launchd misses StartCalendarInterval while the
         laptop is sleeping and DOES NOT auto-catch-up. StartInterval=14400
         (4h) ensures we re-probe shortly after wake. -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>14400</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/YOURUSER/.local/state/schwab-marketdata-mcp/logs/health.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/YOURUSER/.local/state/schwab-marketdata-mcp/logs/health.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
```

> Replace `YOURUSER` with the output of `whoami`.  If you use mise / pyenv,
> point `ProgramArguments[0]` at the absolute path returned by `which uv`.

After loading, run `bash scripts/notifier-self-test.sh` once to confirm
`osascript` actually fires a notification.

---

## Linux (crontab)

Append to `crontab -e`:

```cron
# Schwab MCP token health probe — primary slots (24h clock).
MAILTO=""   # leave empty unless you have sendmail / msmtp configured.
0 20 * * 0 cd "$HOME/code/kevinkda/schwab-marketdata-mcp" && "$HOME/.local/bin/uv" run python -m schwab_marketdata_mcp.health >> "$HOME/.local/state/schwab-marketdata-mcp/logs/health.out.log" 2>> "$HOME/.local/state/schwab-marketdata-mcp/logs/health.err.log"
0 21 * * 3 cd "$HOME/code/kevinkda/schwab-marketdata-mcp" && "$HOME/.local/bin/uv" run python -m schwab_marketdata_mcp.health >> "$HOME/.local/state/schwab-marketdata-mcp/logs/health.out.log" 2>> "$HOME/.local/state/schwab-marketdata-mcp/logs/health.err.log"

# 4h fall-back so we still notice <12h-to-expiry on a workday.
0 */4 * * * cd "$HOME/code/kevinkda/schwab-marketdata-mcp" && "$HOME/.local/bin/uv" run python -m schwab_marketdata_mcp.health >> "$HOME/.local/state/schwab-marketdata-mcp/logs/health.out.log" 2>> "$HOME/.local/state/schwab-marketdata-mcp/logs/health.err.log"
```

If you have `sendmail` / `msmtp` installed, set `MAILTO=you@example.com` —
cron will send the script's stderr output to that address whenever the
probe exits with code 2 (critical).

---

## Why this schedule?

- **Sunday 20:00 / Wednesday 21:00** — the typical "I am at the desk"
  windows for a part-time investor.  Mid-week catches the case where
  Monday's open invalidated something; weekend catches Friday-late drifts.
- **4h fallback** — `launchd` does not back-fill missed
  `StartCalendarInterval` runs across sleep; `crontab` skips closed-laptop
  runs entirely.  The 4-hour `StartInterval` guarantees we catch any drift
  within a quarter-day of waking up.
- **Long lid-close caveat** — if the laptop is closed for >4 h continuously
  (travel, vacation), it is the user's responsibility to manually run
  `uv run python -m schwab_marketdata_mcp.health` after waking.  The README
  documents this explicitly.

---

## Verifying the schedule

```bash
# Run the probe now to populate logs/health.{out,err}.log
uv run python -m schwab_marketdata_mcp.health
echo "exit code: $?"

# Look at the structured log line
tail -1 ~/.local/state/schwab-marketdata-mcp/logs/health.err.log

# Confirm notifier (macOS / Linux only — see notifier-self-test.sh)
bash scripts/notifier-self-test.sh
```
